Sure! To update a break node’s label to `'loopEnd'` (but only if it isn’t already `'loopEnd'`), you can use the `updateBreak` function.  
Just pass in the node you want to modify and the new label. Here’s how you’d call it:

```javascript
// Assume `breakNode` is the stringified representation of your break node
const updatedNode = updateBreak({
  node: breakNode,   // <-- replace with your actual node string
  label: 'loopEnd'
});
```

If the node already has the label `'loopEnd'`, the function will leave it unchanged; otherwise, it will create a new break node with that label and return it. Let me know if you need help formatting the node string or anything else!
